description:
Design a circuit that converts a binary number to its corresponding Gray code representation. The module takes an n-bit binary input and generates an n-bit Gray code output, where the most significant bit of the Gray code is identical to the most significant bit of the binary input, and each subsequent bit of the Gray code is derived by performing an XOR operation between the current and the previous bits of the binary input.
module top_module(
  input [n-1:0] bin,
  output [n-1:0] gray
);

code:
module top_module(
  input [n-1:0] bin,
  output [n-1:0] gray
);parameter n = 4; // number of input bits

assign gray[0] = bin[0];

generate
  genvar i;
  for (i = 1; i < n; i = i + 1) begin : gray_loop
    assign gray[i] = bin[i] ^ bin[i-1];
  end
endgenerate

endmodule

