description:
Design a frequency divider that generates a lower frequency output signal based on an input clock. The module utilizes a shift register of 8 bits to create a feedback mechanism that enables the clock frequency to be divided. The feedback is computed by performing an XOR operation on selected bits of the shift register, and this value is shifted into the register on each rising edge of the clock. The output signal is set to the most significant bit of the shift register, ensuring that it reflects the divided frequency of the input clock signal.
module top_module(
    input clk,
    output reg out
);

code:
module top_module(
    input clk,
    output reg out
);reg [7:0] shift_reg;
reg feedback;

always @(posedge clk) begin
    feedback = shift_reg[0] ^ shift_reg[2] ^ shift_reg[3] ^ shift_reg[7];
    shift_reg = {shift_reg[6:0], feedback};
end

always @(posedge clk or negedge clk) begin
    if (!clk) begin
        out <= 1'b0;
    end else begin
        out <= shift_reg[7];
    end
end

endmodule

