description:
Design a PWM (Pulse Width Modulation) generator that outputs a signal with a variable duty cycle based on an 8-bit input. The module utilizes a clock input running at 100 MHz to create a PWM signal with a frequency of 1 kHz. The output signal, pwm, is high for a proportionate duration of the cycle depending on the duty cycle value, which ranges from 0 to 100%. The counting mechanism and threshold calculation ensure that the output reflects the specified duty cycle by comparing the count value against a dynamically updated threshold derived from the duty cycle input.
module top_module(
  input clk,
  input [7:0] duty_cycle,
  output reg pwm
);

code:
module top_module(
  input clk,
  input [7:0] duty_cycle,
  output reg pwm
);reg [7:0] count;
reg [7:0] threshold;

parameter CLK_FREQ = 100000000; // 100 MHz clock frequency
parameter PWM_FREQ = 1000; // 1 kHz PWM frequency

always @ (posedge clk) begin
  if (count == threshold) begin
    count <= 0;
    pwm <= 1;
  end else if (count == 255) begin
    count <= 0;
    pwm <= 0;
  end else begin
    count <= count + 1;
  end
end

always @ (posedge clk) begin
  threshold <= (duty_cycle * 256) / 100;
end

endmodule

