Design a clock divider that converts a 50 MHz input clock signal to a 1.49 Hz output clock signal. The module uses a 25-bit counter that increments on the rising edge of the 50 MHz clock. When the reset signal is active low, the counter resets to zero. The output clock signal at 1.49 Hz is generated by taking the 25th bit of the counter, effectively providing a significantly reduced clock frequency suitable for timing applications.
module top_module(
    input  clock_50_MHz,
    input  reset_n,
    output clock_1_49_Hz
);

