description:
Design a delay-locked loop (DLL) that synchronizes an input data signal with a reference clock. The module consists of a shift register implemented as a delay line, which stores the incoming data and shifts it on each clock cycle. A phase detector compares the phase of the input data signal and the reference clock to generate a control signal that dynamically adjusts the delay line's output. The final output, `data_out`, is selected from the delay line based on the control signal, ensuring the output data is aligned with the clock, thus facilitating stable data transfer in synchronous systems.
